## Fix Round 1

Date: 2026-08-27

### Status and files

Resolved all three open review findings:

- `core/backtest_engine.py`: moved policy-interface validation into the client cleanup scope; distinguished exactly-full from over-capacity portfolios; admitted an eviction candidate only at exact capacity; and made the allocation safety maxima unconditional literals `0.01` and `0.08`.
- `tests/test_backtest_engine.py`: added lifecycle validation-failure coverage, strengthened the lowered-capacity regression through both signal evaluation and actual entry execution, and added direct-entry regressions for both fixed ceilings.
- `tests/test_backtest_open_causality.py`: normalized only five obsolete unsafe risk/stop fixture inputs. All causality setup and assertions remain unchanged. The no-cash fixture uses `0.01/0.0101`, retaining near-full deployment while keeping the existing entry-day low above its stop; ratio-equivalent `0.008/0.08` values preserve the sizing assertions in the other affected fixtures.

This round supersedes the original report's compatibility statement: there is no longer any direct-entry or injected-strategy exception to the fixed 1% risk and 8% stop-distance ceilings.

